    "content": "The Broadband Equity, Access, and Deployment (BEAD) Program provides $42.45 billion to expand high-speed internet access by funding planning, infrastructure deployment, and adoption programs. Florida received an initial BEAD allocation of $683,057,831. \n\nFlorida's BEAD Initial Proposal Volume I was approved by NTIA on August 14, 2024. Florida's BEAD Initial Proposal Volume II was approved by NTIA on December 19, 2024. Florida submitted its Final Proposal on April 30, 2025.\n\nFlorida received an initial BEAD allocation of $683,057,831. In compliance with NTIA, Florida is committed to deploying the most reliable, least expensive technology with the highest speed, to achieve universal broadband coverage. Florida will ensure appropriate oversight and management of BEAD funds, including compliance with the Build America, Buy America Act and other federal requirements.\n\n\n\nFlorida BEAD Application\nFor this round of BEAD funding, applications are no longer being accepted. Florida's BEAD funding round has been closed.\n\nFlorida BEAD Program\nThe BEAD program is intended to provide service to every unserved and underserved household and business in the state. The Florida BEAD program awarded funds to 10 providers/ISPs awarded as follows:\n\n\n\nGrantee\nAward Amount\nCounty/Ies Served\n10 Gig Internet (dba Fybercom)\nApprox. $26M\nCalhoun, Gulf, Liberty\nAT&T\nApprox. $126M\nMultiple Counties\nComcast\nApprox. $128M\nMultiple Counties\nEarthLink\nApprox. $17M\nMultiple Counties\nFrontier Communications\nApprox. $166M\nMultiple Counties\nKnology (dba WideOpenWest or WOW!)\nApprox. $11M\nMultiple Counties\nLumen\nApprox. $4M\nMultiple Counties\nMediAmerica\nApprox. $4M\nFlagler, Putnam, Volusia\nMetroNet\nApprox. $11M\nMultiple Counties\nSpectrum (Charter Communications)\nApprox. $186M\nMultiple Counties\n\n\nState Broadband Data Collection Tool\n\nState Broadband Data Collection Tool\nThe State Broadband Data Collection Tool (SBDCT) is the state's central repository for collecting broadband data from Florida ISPs.\n\n\n\n\n\nFlorida Department of Economic Opportunity (DEO) / Florida Commerce\n\nWork with us: Careers at DEO\n\nAbout DEO\n\nWork with us: Careers at DEO\n\nFlorida BEAD Program\n\nFollow us:\n\nFacebook\n\nTwitter\n\nLinkedIn\n\nInstagram\n\nYouTube\n\nSign Up for Updates\nEnter your email to receive news and information about BEAD from Florida Commerce."
